  prose: [
    { identity: 'greed turbo farmer, acid spray melts armor and camps, unstable concoction brews into an area stun, corrosive weaponry stacks the chase slow, chemical rage cranks the regen and swing speed', why: 'dedicated pos 1, greed outfarms the map and hits every power spike early, favored into slow farming carry lines, vetoed by the kite and heal cut crew', how: 'spray the camp and the lane, brew the stun before committing, rage the trade and chase the runner, keep the greed stacks rolling on every last hit', when: 'farm lead from the opening minutes, brew tempo and siege windows through the mid game, falls behind the harder scaling carries late', build: 'rad, agh, manta, bkb, assault, bloodthorn, abyssal blade', timings: [['rad', 15], ['agh', 24]], tech: ['ancient apparition, storm spirit, and shadow demon are the vetoes, the ice blast heal cut and the kite crew gut the rage plan', 'sniper, drow ranger, and medusa style farm races are the free wins, greed hits the spikes long before any slow farmer does'], mechanics: [['tip', 'catch them standing in the spray before the stun lands, the armor strip makes the concoction hit far harder'], ['tip', 'the concoction\'s self detonation is lethal, cook it to deny yourself when the gank has you dead'], ['tip', 'start brewing before the teleport and land with the stun fully cooked, only when you are first to the fight'], ['tip', 'chemical rage is a basic dispel on cast, wipe damage over time, slows, blinds, and roots off yourself'], ['tip', 'chemical rage disjoints projectiles on activation, pop it as the spell or attack flies at you'], ['counter', 'the greed multiplies bounty rune gold, contest every spawn or quietly fund his lead']] },
    { identity: 'ranged frost soft support, cold feet freezes the body that stays put, ice vortex slows the lane and amplifies the magic, chilling touch loads the frostbite onto the attacks, ice blast crosses the map to shatter the low health and cut every heal', why: 'dedicated pos 5, the blast answers any fight from anywhere and the shatter caps the sustain cores, favored into the regen lines the heal cut starves, vetoed by the split spreads and the night hunters that run the paper frame down', how: 'vortex the approach and the chase lane, cold feet the slowed body, touch the carry for the frostbite, hold the blast for the fleeing core and the shatter line', when: 'lane pokes off the touch and the vortex zones, mid game the blast turns every enemy sustain fight into a shatter window, falls behind when the dives reach him and the fronts stack the health', build: 'shard, glimmer, blink, gungir, aeon disk, octarine, sheepstick', timings: [['shard', 24], ['glimmer', 26]], tech: ['visage, brewmaster, and night stalker are the vetoes, the split packs spread past the blast and the night vision hunts the paper roam', 'monkey king, gyrocopter, and centaur style clumps are the free wins, the shatter caps the front and the frostbite holds the trade'], mechanics: [['tip', 'ice vortex strips magic resistance inside the ring, carpet the sieges and stack it with the chilling touch damage'], ['tip', 'manual chilling touch on the enemy hero draws no creep aggro, harass through the standing wave'], ['tip', 'the frostbite dot from any blast graze keeps the enemy blink daggers broken for the whole duration'], ['tip', 'lead the blast past the runner, the shatter debuff counts for more than the nuke and the projectile flies slow'], ['counter', 'the frostbite blocks every heal source, lifesteal, fountain regen, and urn charges all fail until the debuff drops'], ['counter', 'walk the long way home at low health, the baited blast on the retreat path is the free shatter for him']] },
    { identity: 'mana burn flash farm carry, blink crosses the map, counterspell returns their spells, mana void detonates the drained pool', why: 'dedicated pos 1, blink farming outpaces the map and the void detonates every drained pool, favored into storm and medusa style mana hoarders, vetoed by lane bullies and the early push crew', how: 'farm between the waves, burn the lane pool, blink the flank, counterspell their opener, void the drained body, split the map when they group', when: 'lane survives on burn trades and blink escapes, spikes once the cleave lands, mid game split farm monster, late game the burn outpaces every pool', build: 'bfury, manta, butterfly, skadi, abyssal blade, bkb, monkey king bar', timings: [['bfury', 14], ['manta', 21]], tech: ['axe, bristleback, and centaur are the vetoes, lane bullies and the instant call stall the farm clock', 'storm spirit, medusa, and leshrac style lines are the free wins, drained pools detonate and the mana hoarding drafts lose the farm race'], mechanics: [['tip', 'blink disjoints any spell or attack projectile already flying at him'], ['tip', 'mana void is not just an execute, the splash off a drained pool shreds the clump and the stun cuts channels'], ['tip', 'tap the treads to intelligence before every blink and back to agility after, the mana saved adds up fast'], ['counter', 'roots and leashes stop the blink cast entirely, hold one ready for him'], ['counter', 'the blink particle trail always floats the direction he traveled, read it and cut the angle'], ['counter', 'never hug an out of mana teammate late, they are the bomb his mana void detonates']] },
    { identity: 'nightmare hard support, enfeeble strangles the carry\'s damage and cast range, brain sap drains and heals him back, nightmare sleeps any body for the setup, fiend\'s grip locks one hero out of the world while it drains the pool', why: 'dedicated pos 5, the grip deletes one enemy core for the whole channel and nightmare turns every roam into a kill setup, favored into immobile cores and saveless lines, vetoed by the instant silence and hex crew', how: 'enfeeble the enemy carry before the fight breaks, sap the lane pool dry, nightmare the runner for the follow up, grip the core from fog and hold the channel to the last tick', when: 'lane sustain off sap trades, nightmare roams land picks through the mid game, grip windows decide the late fights, falls behind when the saves and dispels stack up', build: 'aether lens, glimmer, blink, force, cyclone, agh, shard', timings: [['aether lens', 24], ['glimmer', 27]], tech: ['rubick and the instant silence crew pinch the grip, the steal eats the channel whole', 'ursa, sven, and faceless void style committed cores are the free wins, the grip holds every button they own still'], mechanics: [['tip', 'nightmare grants a beat of invulnerability as it lands, sleep your ally or yourself to dodge the spell already flying'], ['tip', 'bane pounds the sleeper freely with spells and attacks, only fiend\'s grip ends the sleep'], ['tip', 'enfeeble cuts attack damage and cast range in one cast, it strangles the right clicker and the long range caster together'], ['tip', 'brain sap lands straight through bkb and debuff immunity, the sustain never blanks'], ['counter', 'stuns and silences stop the grip channel, strong dispels like aphotic shield and false promise rip it off the victim'], ['tip', 'the scepter spawns grip illusions on both flanks, the hold outlives his own death while either body channels']] },
    { identity: 'track gold soft support that hunts roamers and wins the vision war', why: 'dedicated pos 4, track gold funds the team and wins the vision war, favored into sand king and timber style roamers', how: 'track every kill, hunt their roamer and wards, shuriken the tracked target', when: 'track pressure from level 1, strongest through the early game, rotate with the gold lead', build: 'essence distiller, vessel, ancient janggo, force, pipe, lotus, sheepstick', timings: [['essence distiller', 16], ['vessel', 18]], tech: ['ck and abaddon are the worst lanes, big game hunter stacks the track income', 'invis reveals flip the matchup, buy dust for the mirror and their sentry sweeps'], mechanics: [['tip', 'shuriken bounces to tracked targets, open on a creep so it reaches the distant hero'], ['tip', 'dust reveal and slow linger after leaving the radius, euls or lotus dispels it'], ['counter', 'euls, manta, lotus, greaves, disperser all dispel track, so do allied dispels like aphotic shield'], ['counter', 'track gold makes even trades pay, a 1 for 1 is really 1.5 gold for 1, don\'t coinflip fights into bounty'], ['counter', 'essence distiller gives true sight on the debuffed target, it sees shadow walk']] },
    { identity: 'brawling split offlaner, thunder clap slams the clump, cinder brew soaks the target and ignites on damage, drunken brawler swaps the stances and the fire stance rolls the crits, primal split floods the fight with earth, storm, and fire brewlings', why: 'dedicated pos 3, the split swarms the standing teamfights with brewling bodies and the storm kit picks the commit apart, favored into lancer and naga style illusion floods, vetoed by the instant silence and hex crew', how: 'clap the clump, brew the runner and ignite it, brawl the stance trade, split the commit, cyclone the fed core, hold the storm dispel for the summon flood, walk the storm body out of the lost fight', when: 'lane trades off clap and brew poke, the earth brewling sieges every mid game objective, split windows decide the standing fights, dies to the instant silence that lands before the split', build: 'midas, vessel, rad, assault, bkb, octarine, refresher', timings: [['midas', 12], ['vessel', 13]], tech: ['silencer, skywrath, and disruptor are the vetoes, the instant silence cuts the brew and the clap out of the combo', 'phantom lancer, naga siren, and terrorblade style floods are the free wins, the storm dispel wipes every illusion and summon body'], mechanics: [['tip', 'cinder brew soaks the enemies and slows them, magic or pure damage lights the soak and the burn runs longer'], ['tip', 'the fire stance crit is rolled the moment the swing starts, swapping into fire mid swing never crits that hit'], ['tip', 'auras ride whichever brewling currently leads, the order runs earth, then storm, then fire as each falls, and brewmaster walks back out wherever that body stands'], ['tip', 'the earth brewling\'s demolish passive shreds buildings, it is the siege body, push every objective behind it'], ['tip', 'the storm cyclone outlasts the split itself, and it holds creeps and summons in the air far longer than heroes'], ['tip', 'storm dispel magic shreds summons, illusions eat the full damage, clones, tombstone zombies, and ward type bodies are the exceptions'], ['counter', 'kill the fire brewling first, it swings the hardest and burns everything near it, deleting it strips most of the split\'s damage'], ['counter', 'primal split has a long cast time, instant silences and hexes land first and cut the combo down to the split alone']] },
    { identity: 'raid boss offlane core that returns every hit, stomps the fight open and stampedes the whole team through', why: 'offlane tank that outlanes melee cores, the return damage taxes every right click and the big ult turns any retreat or chase, vetoed by carapace reflects and break windows', how: 'soak harass with the return, shove lanes with the free nuke, initiate on the clump and stampede the team through', when: 'spikes when the ult and initiator tempo land mid game, falls off when enemy damage outscales the health pool', build: 'helm of the dominator, blade mail, heart, pipe, lotus, shiva, bkb', timings: [['helm of the dominator', 9], ['blade mail', 20]], tech: ['viper, drow, and nyx are the vetoes, range and carapace turn the return against him', 'ursa, troll, and monkey king style melee carries are the free wins, they feed the return all game'], mechanics: [['tip', 'double edge costs no mana at all, spam it as the free nuke for pushing and wave clear'], ['tip', 'stampede speeds every allied hero and summon on the map, and every stampeding body applies the slow'], ['tip', 'hitch a ride makes the carried ally fully invulnerable, damage, debuffs, even the chrono arena cannot touch them'], ['counter', 'flak cannon, glaive, and split shot splashes only trigger the return when centaur is the primary target'], ['counter', 'nyx carapace reflects the return off a plain right click, auto attacking him just hands him free stuns'], ['counter', 'silver edge breaks the return passive and caps his move speed, the stampede escape dies under it']] },
    { identity: 'skeleton tempo carry, searing arrows burn every click, strafe stacks the attack steroid, skeleton walk fades him across the map and plants the archer turrets, death pact eats a body to bulk up', why: 'dedicated pos 1, the walk tempo and the arrow spam outfarm the lane and the strafe window deletes the backline before it responds, favored into sniper and drow style immobile backs, vetoed by the blink lockdown crew', how: 'searing arrow every last hit and deny, walk the flank through fog, plant the archers on the high ground, strafe the commit onto the backline, pact a creep between trades, walk out when the steroid ends', when: 'lane pest off arrow harass, the archer turrets add standing damage to every push, mid game pick machine off the walk cooldowns, dies the moment the blink lockdown lands on him', build: 'falcon blade, desolator, pike, daedalus, bkb, monkey king bar, sheepstick', timings: [['falcon blade', 5], ['desolator', 15]], tech: ['axe, earthshaker, and sand king are the vetoes, the blink lockdown crew deletes him before strafe pays', 'sniper, drow ranger, and crystal maiden style backs are the free wins, the walk flank reaches everything that cannot leap'], mechanics: [['tip', 'death pact can eat an enemy creep or your own skeleton archer, it heals him and pads his max health'], ['tip', 'skeleton archers copy his attack range exactly and swing for a share of his attack damage, both track his stats live'], ['tip', 'the archers spawn the instant skeleton walk drops and they never move, aim the walk exit to perch them on cliffs for scouting vision'], ['tip', 'cast skeleton walk mid channel without breaking it, strafe and death pact cast during the walk keep the invis, attacks and item use pop it'], ['tip', 'the shard barrage arrows fly with true strike, carry every attack modifier, and still fire while clinkz is disarmed'], ['counter', 'dispelling strafe off clinkz is wasted effort, the skeleton archers keep their share of the buff'], ['counter', 'damage block never blunts skeleton archer shots, their hits ignore it entirely']] },
    { identity: 'offlane illusion front, vacuum drags the fight into one spot, ion shell grinds the lane and the chase, surge pushes any body to top speed through the slows, wall of replica floods the fight with enemy copies', why: 'dedicated pos 3, one vacuum sets every aoe follow up and the wall cashes the enemy cores against them, favored into the ranged paper fronts, vetoed by the spread lines and the dispel crew', how: 'shell the wave and the front liner, vacuum the clump into the follow up, surge the runner or the initiator, wall the engage path before the fight breaks', when: 'shell owns the lane trades from the start, mid game the vacuum turns every objective into the combo window, late the wall copies carry the fight, falls behind when the drafts refuse the clump', build: 'mekansm, shiva, pipe, lotus, shard, bkb, sheepstick', timings: [['mekansm', 19], ['shiva', 23]], tech: ['oracle and bounty hunter are the vetoes, the dispel strips the shell and the track hunts the vacuum engages', 'shadow fiend, drow ranger, and templar assassin lines are the free wins, the ranged paper fronts feed the wall copies'], mechanics: [['tip', 'ion shell casts on enemy bodies too, shell their melee at the tower and force the wave or the retreat'], ['tip', 'shell the second or third body in the wave, the frontline creep eats the enemy hits and dies first'], ['tip', 'surge and shell the allied init more than yourself, the lasso and the charge stretch miles under the speed'], ['tip', 'micro the wall copies onto the priority target, their default orders waste the replicas on nothing'], ['counter', 'the shell on a creep puts his lane spell on cooldown, punish the cooldown window with harass'], ['counter', 'ion shell dispels clean off, the fortune\'s end and the convert style dispels gut the lane plan']] },
    { identity: 'tanky offlane initiator with global solar guardian ult presence', why: 'dedicated offlane brick, the global ult turns every fight into a 6v5, favored into SF style immobile mids', how: 'starbreaker lane trades, hammer into fights from anywhere, front line for your carry', when: 'lane brick early, ult windows all game, mid game monster once blade mail and harpoon land', build: 'blade mail, shard, harpoon, desolator, bkb, assault, abyssal blade', timings: [['blade mail', 18], ['shard', 22]], tech: ['visage and chen veto, nyx burns the ult economy', 'channel the global from fog, never in range of their stun'], mechanics: [['tip', 'blink forward after the opening swipes to land the final starbreaker stun on top of a target'], ['tip', 'solar guardian stun pierces bkb, debuff immune enemies still eat the landing'], ['tip', 'once airborne she is invulnerable and hidden, nothing interrupts the landing, damage lands just before the stun'], ['counter', 'silence cannot cancel a started starbreaker, stuns, sleeps, and fears all can'], ['counter', 'nyx walks into solar guardian with carapace up and reflects the whole landing']] },
    { identity: 'swarm tempo offlaner, crypt swarm waves the lane down, silence cuts the casters out of the trade, spirit siphon drains the front body and feeds her back, witchcraft deepens the move speed and the cooldowns as she levels, exorcism floods the fight with ghosts that strip the structures and pay the heal at the end', why: 'dedicated pos 3, the swarm and the silence hold the tempo and the exorcism takes every objective on cooldown, favored into the paper frames and the refraction lines, vetoed by the rupture and the heal cut crew', how: 'wave the lane down with the swarm, silence the caster mid combo, siphon the front body for the sustain, pop the exorcism on the objective and stand close so the ghosts cycle, retarget them onto the runner through the disables', when: 'swarm poke from the opening ranks, the siphon holds every lane trade, mid game exorcism windows siege every tower, late the ghosts and the heal grind the long fights, starves when the heal cuts and the silence answers stack up', build: 'consecrated wraps, kaya and sange, blink, lotus, bkb, shiva, shard', timings: [['consecrated wraps', 17], ['kaya and sange', 23]], tech: ['bloodseeker is the veto, the rupture holds the waddle and the thirst true sights the retreat', 'shadow fiend, templar assassin, and venomancer style lines are the free wins, the ghosts sweep the plague wards, the paper frames feed the heal'], mechanics: [['tip', 'ground target the swarm onto the juking body, the unit targeted cast cancels when they break vision'], ['tip', 'several siphons run at once but never two on one body, drain every chaser when the gank lands'], ['tip', 'the siphon heal ignores the magic resist, the siege creeps and the golems pay the full sustain'], ['tip', 'the siphon drains roshan and the tormentor too'], ['tip', 'the exorcism ghosts deal physical damage, the enemy armor decides the payout'], ['tip', 'the exorcism ghosts follow her right clicks, retarget them through the stuns and the cyclone'], ['counter', 'never chase her through the standing exorcism, the ghosts refill her health when the cast ends'], ['counter', 'the health restoration cuts trim the siphon and the exorcism heal']] },
    { identity: 'devour offlane core that eats the map for tempo, burns heroes down with the infernal blade and vetoes a carry with the doom', why: 'tank core that outlasts the lane, the ult vetoes one enemy hero for a whole fight, favored into enigma and tidehunter style ult dependent heroes, vetoed by self dispels and long range kite', how: 'devour for gold and creep spells, bully the lane with the burn, then doom the enemy carry at the start of every fight', when: 'strong once the ult and initiator tempo come online mid game, falls off when enemy saves and dispels arrive late', build: 'ancient janggo, midas, rad, shard, bkb, shiva, octarine', timings: [['ancient janggo', 11], ['midas', 13]], tech: ['slark and lifestealer are the vetoes, self dispels and rage shrug the ult off', 'storm and enigma are the free wins, one doom deletes their whole fight plan'], mechanics: [['tip', 'devour only pays the bonus gold when the digest buff runs out, budget it as unreliable income'], ['tip', 'the ult silences, dispels the target on cast, and freezes their health so every heal source fails'], ['tip', 'self cast the scepter ult and it never curses you, you just walk around wearing the doom as an aura'], ['counter', 'click him before the fight, the devoured spell swaps his kit, a hidden war stomp or the wolf aura flips the engage'], ['counter', 'if he opens with the burn and holds no devoured cancel, tp out fast, the burn is his only lockdown']] },
    { identity: 'lane brick that counters magic mids', why: 'counter pick into puck and TA, dragon blood blanks magic harass', how: 'win lane by existing, stun their carry out of elder form, take towers behind it', when: 'lane brick early, mid game tower monster in elder form', build: 'rad, bkb, octarine, shiva, bloodthorn, assault, overwhelming blink', timings: [['rad', 19], ['bkb', 25]], tech: ['break and heal cut turn dragon blood off, viper and huskar are the veto cluster'], mechanics: [['tip', 'breathe fire cuts total attack damage including bonus damage from items, use it early in the fight'], ['tip', 'corrosive breath burn works on towers, the dot is the whole early push package'], ['tip', 'the transform itself is the gank, nobody respects the instant ranged stun out of knight form'], ['counter', 'silver edge and viper strike carry the break, dragon blood regen goes with it'], ['counter', 'vessel, skadi, ice blast, doom, even withering mist all cut the dragon blood regen']] },
    { identity: 'blink initiator soft support, fissure cuts the lane and the fight in half, enchant totem primes the burst, aftershock pays a stun behind every cast, echo slam cashes the clump', why: 'dedicated pos 4, one fissure sets every kill and the slam flips every clumped fight, favored into the illusion and summon lines that stack the payout, the spread drafts and the battery assault crew blunt him', how: 'block the runner with the fissure, walk in on a primed totem, blink the clump and slam, chain the aftershock stuns with one click between casts, stun off the lingering fissures once the shard lands', when: 'fissure controls the lanes from level one, the blink turns every clumped objective into a slam window, mid game the combo deletes the paper cores, falls off when the enemy spreads and the bkbs arrive', build: 'blink, shard, force, yasha and kaya, bkb, octarine, refresher', timings: [['blink', 16], ['shard', 23]], tech: ['clockwerk is the veto, the battery cancels most of the combo, only the slam is safe', 'shadow fiend, anti mage, and nature prophet lines are the free wins, the summons and the paper frames stack the slam'], mechanics: [['tip', 'any unit his spells kill flies backwards and deals damage on the way, the slugger innate taxes the clumped retreat'], ['tip', 'the fissure block is often worth more than the stun, lead the long casts ahead and never cut the team off the target'], ['tip', 'do not mash the combo, one right click fits between the casts once aftershock is maxed'], ['tip', 'the shard puts aftershock on every lingering fissure from anywhere, stun off the old cracks mid fight'], ['tip', 'echo slam hits the invisible in full, the smoke and the meld give no shelter'], ['tip', 'echo slam carries no cast animation, it lands as long as he is not disabled'], ['counter', 'clockwerk breaks the combo, the battery assault cancels most of the cast animations, the slam still lands'], ['counter', 'aftershock never triggers under break, the silver edge guts the chain'], ['counter', 'roots pin the scepter totem jump in place']] },
    { identity: 'convert tempo hard support, enchant takes the big neutral and turns the map, impetus taxes every retreat by the gap it leaves, untouchable slows the right clicks into bullet time, natures attendants keep the front alive', why: 'dedicated pos 5, the convert owns the early rotations and the impetus scales the whole game off positioning, favored into the jakiro and prophet lines, marci and the gap closing dives dump her through the slow', how: 'convert the biggest neutral and siege behind it, impetus the retreating bodies from max range, dispel the enemy buffs with the point blank enchant, sproink the projectiles and keep the gap open', when: 'converts own the first ten minutes, mid game the impetus punishes every rotation, late the untouchable tanks roshan while the paper frames melt, starves when the breaks and the burst answers land', build: 'ancient janggo, essence distiller, glimmer, agh, orchid, shard, pike', timings: [['ancient janggo', 15], ['essence distiller', 16]], tech: ['marci is the veto, the rebound closes the gap she lives on and the dispose dumps her', 'jakiro, nature prophet, and shadow fiend lines are the free wins, the paper frames pay the impetus'], mechanics: [['tip', 'manual impetus on a hero draws no creep aggro, harass through the standing wave'], ['tip', 'impetus pays the distance when the arrow lands, capped at 1750'], ['tip', 'enchant converts nearly every unit including illusions, never the creep heroes, the brewlings, the golems, and the familiars stay theirs'], ['tip', 'enchant on a hero dispels first, the aphotic shield, the surge, the ion shell, and the jingu buffs wipe off'], ['tip', 'untouchable tanks roshan, he swings in bullet time'], ['tip', 'the shard sproink disjoints the incoming projectiles'], ['counter', 'walk into her to cut the impetus payout, the damage counts the gap when the arrow lands'], ['counter', 'breaks strip untouchable, the silver edge, the vendetta, and the viper strike turn her paper again'], ['counter', 'untouchable bites through bkb and debuff immunity'], ['counter', 'the enemy jungle camps swing harder under her rabble rouser innate']] },
    { identity: 'ranged offlaner with demonic conversion eidolon pushing, midnight pulse zones, and a black hole ultimate that wins teamfights', why: 'black hole wins the teamfight game, favored into BS and troll style clumped drafts, eidolons push the map', how: 'eidolon lane pressure and tower sieges, midnight zones, blink bkb hole the stack', when: 'eidolon push through the early game, hole windows every fight once blink and bkb land', build: 'ancient janggo, midas, blink, bkb, octarine, shiva, refresher', timings: [['ancient janggo', 7], ['midas', 12]], tech: ['lycan and meepo veto, unit flood overruns the eidolons', 'count their hole cancels before locking, a stack of rubick, sd, charge, or long silences means no enigma'], mechanics: [['tip', 'midnight pulse chews trees in a huge aoe, it burns sprout and knocks a tree dancing mk off his perch'], ['tip', 'midnight pulse deals full damage through bkb and debuff immunity, bkbd targets still melt in the zone'], ['tip', 'spawn multiplied eidolons before a solo early black hole, the channel alone doesn\'t have the damage'], ['tip', 'black hole silences on top of the stun, abaddon can\'t manually pop borrowed time and ursa can\'t enrage out'], ['counter', 'primal roar, global silence, overgrowth, and rubick steal all cancel hole through debuff immunity, count them first'], ['counter', 'walking away from a close range enigma eats an event horizon slow, respect the innate when disengaging']] },
    { identity: 'tree hopping squirrel support, acorn shot plants the tree and bounces the instant attack, bushwhack nets the bodies to the trunk and stuns them, scurry skates the tree lines, sharpshooter winds the unstoppable shot that slows and breaks', why: 'dedicated pos 4, the bushwhack cashes every tree on the map into a stun and the sharpshooter snipes the runner from fog, favored into the paper lanes and the rooted casters, vetoed by the tree cutters and the flood lines', how: 'acorn the tree beside the target, bushwhack the net onto it, scurry the tree line for the reset, hold the sharpshooter for the committed fight and juke the recoil across the cliffs', when: 'tree hugger trades from the opening ranks, mid roams land the bushwhack picks, late the sharpshooter break guts the carries, starves when the lanes hold no trees', build: 'essence distiller, glimmer, aether lens, blink, shard, gungir, sheepstick', timings: [['essence distiller', 15], ['glimmer', 26]], tech: ['visage, spirit breaker, and bounty hunter are the vetoes, the familiars flood the tree lines and the hunt crew runs the paper frame down', 'shadow fiend, tiny, and alchemist style paper farms are the free wins, the greed races and the rooted frames stand in the acorn poke and eat the bushwhack'], mechanics: [['tip', 'keep the mistwoods wayfarer innate on by hugging trees, the survivability lives in the tree line'], ['tip', 'the acorn tree carries collision, plant it behind you to shove yourself out of the kinetic field and the pounce leash'], ['tip', 'nothing interrupts a sharpshooter windup except the cancel or death, stuns and silences ride it out'], ['tip', 'spells and items keep casting through the sharpshooter windup, aimed only along the shot line'], ['counter', 'destroying the tree a hero is bushwhacked to cancels the stun instantly, cut the trunk to free the target'], ['counter', 'the sharpshooter debuff wipes off with a basic dispel, the slow and the break never hold']] },
    { identity: 'melee carry whose blade fury spin shrugs off spells, whose healing ward sustains every push, whose blade dance crits scale the right clicks, and whose omnislash leaps between targets untouchable', why: 'dedicated pos 1, the spin blanks the magic burst and the slash isolates the locked target, favored into NP, centaur, and SF lines', how: 'spin the magic trade, ward the siege, crit the tank, omnislash the isolated target or the diving core', when: 'strong level gates through the mid game with the ward sustaining every push, dips into the kiting floods before the late items land', build: 'bfury, manta, butterfly, monkey king bar, skadi, swift blink, blessing', timings: [['bfury', 14], ['manta', 22]], tech: ['OD, night stalker, and spirit breaker are the vetoes, the astral and the hunt blank the spin economy', 'NP, centaur, and SF lines are the free wins, the slash and the spin punish everything that commits close'], mechanics: [['tip', 'blade fury does not interrupt his channeling, spin mid tp and the escape channel holds'], ['tip', 'casting the spin is a basic dispel, the debuffs riding him wipe off as the storm starts'], ['tip', 'the storm negates his own attack damage, the spin is the damage and the sword waits it out'], ['tip', 'mid omnislash he still casts items and spells, the spin alone is locked out of the slash'], ['counter', 'the slash hunts a short radius around him, outrun the jump range and the chain cuts early'], ['counter', 'the healing ward dies to one hit and heals their whole team, kill it the moment it lands']] },
    { identity: 'frog bard offlaner, catchy lick buffs the pair or dispels the threat, frogstomp stamps the ground control, croak of genius conducts the damage, the healing, or the speed, amphibian rhapsody swings the committed fight with the adaptive chorus', why: 'dedicated pos 3, the lick flips every spell trade and the rhapsody answers their biggest fight, favored into the tanky fronts that stand in the stomp, vetoed by the silence chains that never let the chorus run', how: 'lick the threatened ally or the winning threat, stomp the engage path, croak the buff the fight needs, hold the rhapsody for the committed clump', when: 'lane trades flip on the lick from the early ranks, mid game the stomp owns every choke, late the rhapsody turns their all in, falls behind when the burst reaches him first', build: 'meteor hammer, kaya and sange, octarine, lotus, shard, bkb, shiva', timings: [['meteor hammer', 17], ['kaya and sange', 23]], tech: ['enigma, grimstroke, anti mage, and outworld destroyer are the vetoes, the hole, the soulbind, and the mana drains starve the chorus', 'drow ranger, shadow fiend, mars, and ember spirit are the free wins, the paper frames and the brawlers stand in the stomp'], mechanics: [['tip', 'catchy lick is a basic dispel that lands on enemies, allies, and largo himself, one lick answers both directions'], ['tip', 'the lick drag interrupts skewer, icarus dive, charge of darkness, and blast off'], ['tip', 'frogstomp and the rhapsody blitz damage hit invisible and fogged bodies, no dust needed to clear the fog runners'], ['counter', 'the lick turns you to face him, never panic leap or heavenly jump after the lick lands or you dive deeper'], ['counter', 'croak of genius wipes off with a basic dispel, eul and nullifier peel the reverb off your backs']] },
    { identity: 'pulse nova siege mid, split earth cracks the delayed stun, lightning storm bounces the wave down, diabolic edict melts towers, pulse nova grinds every fight that stands still', why: 'dedicated pos 2, edict and nova outtempo every tower race and the nova zone wins the clumped fights, favored into lifestealer and lancer style melee floods, vetoed by the gap close dive', how: 'split earth where they will stand not where they stand, storm the bounce off the wave, edict the tower behind the push, nova on and walk the fight, split earth the escape line', when: 'lane bully off storm and earth poke, edict sieges every mid game objective, nova carries the standing fights, dies to the gap close that lands first', build: 'kaya and sange, yasha and kaya, bkb, bloodstone, shiva, sheepstick, shard', timings: [['kaya and sange', 23], ['yasha and kaya', 24]], tech: ['storm spirit, spirit breaker, and slark are the vetoes, the dive deletes the frame before nova pays', 'lifestealer, phantom lancer, and broodmother style floods are the free wins, the nova grinds every body that commits close'], mechanics: [['tip', 'split earth carries one of the longest windups around, bait the dodge in lane by canceling the cast, or drop it at your own feet to stun chasers without turning around'], ['tip', 'edict explosions follow leshrac and land on anything near him including towers, fewer targets means more hits each, hug the edge so the tower eats every blast and skip the right clicks to keep it on the creeps'], ['tip', 'edict keeps exploding around his corpse after he dies, dying mid siege still cracks the tower'], ['tip', 'edict and pulse nova both hit invisible and fogged units, chase the invis runner on a predictable path and the explosions draw him for you'], ['tip', 'lightning storm\'s heavy slow holds them in place, bolt first and split earth lands clean'], ['counter', 'split earth is among the easiest stuns to sidestep, the windup telegraphs it, a small sidestep or a step back dodges the rocks'], ['counter', 'dispel leshrac while the scepter nihilism runs and the whole ethereal aura collapses on the spot']] },
    { identity: 'frost control hard support, frost blast chills and nukes the clump, frost shield armors the siege and burns the melee dive, sinister gaze drags the runner, chain frost bounces the fight apart', why: 'hard support lane anchor, blast spam wins the harass war and shield taxes every dive, chain frost deletes the clumped fights, favored into lancer and terrorblade style illusion floods, vetoed by long range spam and the storm dive', how: 'blast the clump and the ranged creep, shield the sieged core or the tower, gaze the runner into the team after their stuns land, chain frost the clump, never gaze into their interrupt', when: 'lane poke from the first blast ranks, shield holds every tower siege, chain frost windows decide the mid fights, late the shield still blanks the right click dives', build: 'glimmer, blink, solar crest, shard, force, aether lens, aeon disk', timings: [['glimmer', 22], ['blink', 23]], tech: ['zeus, sniper, and storm spirit are the vetoes, the long range spam and the dive outtrade the waddle', 'phantom lancer, terrorblade, and lifestealer style melee floods are the free wins, chain frost and the shield eat everything that commits close'], mechanics: [['tip', 'the sacrifice innate eats an allied creep, its health becomes his mana and he pockets the experience bounty'], ['tip', 'frost shield blunts right clicks and instant attacks of every kind, spell damage and tower shots pass right through'], ['tip', 'frost shield lands on creeps, ward type bodies, and every tower and building, shield the objective under siege'], ['tip', 'the sinister gaze drag ignores pathing, victims walk straight over cliffs and terrain, pull them off the high ground or onto your side of it'], ['tip', 'sinister gaze is a hard disable in practice, the victim cannot act, self casting any save is off the table while it runs'], ['tip', 'spell block only swallows the first chain frost hit, the orb keeps bouncing and keeps growing after'], ['counter', 'the gaze drag reels you a long stretch toward lich, getting caught means walking straight into his team, keep your distance before it starts'], ['counter', 'frost shield and the gaze drag both wipe off with a basic dispel, carry one against him']] },
    { identity: 'melee carry with rage spell immunity, feast percent lifesteal, and infest dives through allies', why: 'dedicated pos 1, feast eats tanks and rage blanks their disables, favored into SF and gyro style farmers', how: 'rage their disables, feast the tank, open wounds the chase, infest an ally to dive or escape', when: 'lane bully from levels, armlet spike in the early mid game, monster late with rad and manta online', build: 'rad, armlet, sange and yasha, manta, assault, monkey king bar, abyssal blade', timings: [['rad', 16], ['armlet', 19]], tech: ['enigma, visage, leshrac, and riki veto, unit flood and the kite blank the feast plan', 'SF and gyro style farmers are the free wins, lanes well beside bounty roam or enigma setups'], mechanics: [['tip', 'rage\'s debuff immunity prevents the tormentor\'s damage reflect'], ['tip', 'infest applies a rare dispel that also wipes buffs, infesting right after a rune loses the rune buff'], ['counter', 'ghost scepter, force, blink, and shiva\'s kite him, a tp scroll saves you until the basher lands'], ['counter', 'break shuts off ghoul frenzy and feast together, silver edge, khanda, and viper strike carry it']] },
    { identity: 'twin-hero carry controlling spirit bear for pushing and item slots, relentless lane pressure', why: 'entangle goes through escape buttons, bear tower damage ends games before farmers come online, favored into drow and void', how: 'bear lane pressure on both last hits, entangle locks the escape, siege with the bear tanking', when: 'strongest early to mid pushing towers, win before the late game when farmers outscale', build: 'mjollnir, silver edge, shard, bkb, butterfly, monkey king bar, blessing', timings: [['mjollnir', 17], ['silver edge', 30]], tech: ['omni and visage veto', 'drow and void are the free wins, entangle through the escape button'], mechanics: [['tip', 'killing the bear pays nothing permanent, cull, flesh heap, and silencer int steal all whiff on it'], ['tip', 'savage roar is stun silence and mute in one, it stops bkb pops, borrowed time, and ursa enrage'], ['tip', 'shard roar dispels a cyclone or silence, cast it from whichever of you or the bear isn\'t disabled'], ['tip', 'shard fetch roots but never disarms, the fetched target keeps right clicking you'], ['counter', 'a suddenly full hp bear means a fresh spawn, kill the druid while he\'s bearless and his lane is over'], ['counter', 'minus armor melts the bear easiest, desolator and cuirass are the standard buys against ld']] },
    { identity: 'moonlight bounce carry, lucent beam snipes and ministuns, moon glaives ricochet through the wave, lunar blessing arms the whole team, eclipse drops the night and the beams together', why: 'dedicated pos 1, glaive bounce clears waves and shreds clumped fights while the beam ministuns hold runners, favored into clumped and summon heavy lines, vetoed by the gap close dive crew', how: 'beam the stun onto the runner, ride the bounce through their clump, keep the blessing beside your team, eclipse the fight that commits', when: 'lane poke off beam spam, mid game bounce and eclipse windows, monster once the bounce damage and the orbiting glaives stack up', build: 'mask of madness, manta, butterfly, bkb, daedalus, swift blink, satanic', timings: [['mask of madness', 10], ['manta', 18]], tech: ['axe, earthshaker, and storm spirit are the vetoes, the blink lockdown and the dive reach her before the bounce pays', 'meepo, broodmother, and lifestealer style floods are the free wins, the glaive bounce shreds every clumped body'], mechanics: [['tip', 'the blessing aura counts creep-hero bodies as heroes, brewlings and familiars ride the damage too'], ['tip', 'her night vision outranges nearly every hero, at the vision edge at night you see them and they do not see you'], ['tip', 'the orbiting glaive strikes carry true strike and ignore disarms entirely'], ['tip', 'glaive bounces count as spell damage yet damage block still trims every bounce'], ['counter', 'once the tier three falls the glaives bounce through every base structure, an errant bounce breaks your blink'], ['counter', 'summons and illusions tank the eclipse beams, feed bodies into the storm instead of your carry']] },
    { identity: 'pack push offlaner, summoned wolves scout and siege, howl shreds the armor and the swing of every enemy near him and his pack, feral impulse feeds every body he controls, shapeshift runs the pack at unslowable haste with the crits', why: 'dedicated pos 3, the wolves take towers while the enemy farms and the night howl strips every fight on the map, favored into the passive farm lines and the slow only kite crews, vetoed by the curse crew that feeds him to his own pack', how: 'scout and siege with the wolves, howl the defenders as the fight breaks, run the shapeshift pack through the runner, hand the spare wolf form to the diving core', when: 'wolf pressure from the opening minutes, tower sieges and the night howl windows through the mid game, shapeshift commits decide the late fights, falls behind when the clear and the lockdown stack up', build: 'helm dom, shard, assault, bkb, agh, nullifier, blink', timings: [['helm dom', 15], ['shard', 18]], tech: ['winter wyvern is the veto, the curse turns his own pack into the executioners, the enchantress scepter little friends ride the wolves late', 'viper and drow ranger style slow kite lines are the free wins, the wolf run ignores every slow they hold'], mechanics: [['tip', 'the wolves sit permanently invisible, a follow command tails a priority target without attacking, free scouting on demand'], ['tip', 'howl works on roshan, the armor and damage strip applies inside the pit'], ['tip', 'the howl debuff goes global at night, one cast strips every enemy on the map'], ['tip', 'a bitten ally returning from banish collects the shapeshift health bonus again, phase shifts and doppelgangers heal on every return'], ['counter', 'the shapeshift run ignores slows entirely, stuns and the cyclone crew hold the wolf down, silver edge caps the run'], ['counter', 'winter curse turns his own pack into the executioners, the wolf plan feeds itself']] },
    { identity: 'melee brawler mid, dispose grabs and hurls any body behind her, rebound leaps off allies into the landing stun, bodyguard shares the shield and the lifesteal, unleash flurries through the committed fight', why: 'dedicated pos 2, every roaming ally becomes a kill setup for the leap and the throwback, favored into immobile paper mids, vetoed by the root crew', how: 'leap off the ranged creep into the wave, throw the target back into the team, shield the diving core, unleash inside the brawl', when: 'lane tempo off the pair setups from the opening ranks, mid roams land the throw picks, mid game brawls feed the flurry windows, falls behind when the roots and the kite stack up', build: 'bkb, blink, shard, daedalus, nullifier, monkey king bar, abyssal blade', timings: [['bkb', 23], ['blink', 24]], tech: ['crystal maiden, dark willow, and treant are the vetoes, the roots blank the rebound and the planted body dies', 'sniper, zeus, and shadow fiend style immobile mids are the free wins, the leap and the throw reach every paper body'], mechanics: [['tip', 'the dispose throw counts as a stun, it breaks enemy channels mid cast'], ['tip', 'the dispose throw runs shorter uphill and longer downhill, map height bends the distance'], ['tip', 'the rebound leap still fires when the target dies mid dash, the corpse carries you'], ['tip', 'enemies cannot see the unleash pulses while she sits in fog, the damage still lands'], ['counter', 'roots and leashes stop the rebound cast entirely, hold one ready for her dash'], ['counter', 'a started rebound only stops for forced movement and knockback, she eats the stun and keeps flying']] },
    { identity: 'arrow hunt soft support, sacred arrow snipes long range stuns from fog, starstorm showers the closest cluster, leap hops cliffs, moonlight veils the team', why: 'soft support playmaker, favored into jakiro and void spirit lines, vetoed by arc warden clones and bounty tracks, arrows decide picks before fights start', how: 'arrow the fog lines beside their stun, starstorm the trade, leap the cliff, quiver poke without creep aggro, veil the team for the engage', when: 'lane arrow threat from the start, mid roams land the long stun, late moonlight ghost starts the engage', build: 'essence distiller, vessel, mekansm, blink, lotus, shard, wind waker', timings: [['essence distiller', 14], ['vessel', 18]], tech: ['arc warden, io, and bounty hunter are the vetoes, clones and track reveal gut the invis value', 'jakiro, void spirit, and shadow fiend style lines are the free wins, clumped paper bodies eat free arrows'], mechanics: [['tip', 'the starstorm follow-up meteor strikes the nearest target and hits fogged units, blind cast it to finish jukers'], ['tip', 'arrow damage and stun scale with travel distance and peak at half max range, skip the max range greed'], ['tip', 'the arrow instantly kills the first creep it hits, snipe big neutrals and siege creeps for free gold'], ['tip', 'the arrow grants flying vision while flying and brief vision on impact, use it to scout fog'], ['tip', 'leap crosses cliffs and impassable terrain, save the charges for real escapes over panic hops'], ['counter', 'moonlight shadow re-fades every ally invis for the full duration, stock sentries and dust before pushing']] },
    { identity: 'tree hopping staff carry, boundless strike sweeps the arc as an instant attack, jingu mastery stacks the hits into the damage and lifesteal buff, tree dance perches him over the lane and primal spring leaps the gap, mischief disguises him as anything standing, wukong\'s command rings the fight with soldiers', why: 'dedicated pos 1, the perch rules the vision war and the jingu lifesteal loops every trade while the soldier ring taxes the whole fight, favored into paper backlines that hold no answer for the perch, vetoed by the tree cutters and the illusion flood', how: 'stack the jingu on the laner, boundless the clump for the buff payout, perch the tree for vision and spring the channel onto the fight, mischief the reset, ring the soldiers around the objective and fight inside them', when: 'lane wins the jingu trade war from the first ranks, perch vision and spring picks through the mid game, the soldier ring carries every standing fight and siege, dies the moment the tree cutters stack up', build: 'bfury, rad, desolator, harpoon, bkb, skadi, monkey king bar', timings: [['bfury', 15], ['rad', 17]], tech: ['enigma and keeper of the light are the vetoes, the midnight pulse and the scepter wisp cut the perch trees out from under the plan, the night stalker skies and the lancer flood pinch the jingu stacks', 'puck, batrider, and drow ranger style paper lines are the free wins, the jingu lifesteal loops every trade and the soldier ring outlasts the paper bodies'], mechanics: [['tip', 'boundless strike is an instant attack with true strike, it lands through disarms and carries every attack modifier but cleave across the arc'], ['tip', 'one boundless sweep spends a single jingu stack, low on health smack the whole wave and the lifesteal pays off every body hit'], ['tip', 'mischief hides him from the enemy minimap and drops tower and creep aggro, the first beat of the disguise is damage immune'], ['tip', 'the wukong soldiers never roll bash or echo sabre procs, every other on hit effect rides their swings and they carry his auras'], ['tip', 'the changing of the guard swap disjoints incoming projectiles and holds him invulnerable for the flight'], ['counter', 'cutting the tree under the perch stuns him for a long beat, the wild axes and midnight pulse crew catch the mid hop dancer'], ['counter', 'basic dispels rip the jingu buff off, fortune\'s end and the demonic purge strip the sustain']] },
    { identity: 'global split push carry, teleport lands anywhere on the map, sprout traps and scouts, treants swarm lanes, wrath bounces the map', why: 'dedicated carry, favored into anti mage and sven lines, vetoed by dragon knight shell and night stalker skies', how: 'teleport behind the undefended lane, sprout the defender, treant the wave, wrath the map and never stop moving', when: 'lane weak without backup, mid game map pressure everywhere, late game race wins with global pressure', build: 'mjollnir, pike, bkb, butterfly, daedalus, monkey king bar, satanic', timings: [['mjollnir', 16], ['pike', 24]], tech: ['dragon knight, night stalker, and phantom lancer are the vetoes, push answers and illusion spam blunt the split', 'anti mage, sven, and ogre magi style lines are the free wins, slow farmers lose the map race'], mechanics: [['tip', 'sprout grants flying vision around the point, scout fog jukes and cliff wards with it'], ['tip', 'sprout can be ground targeted, trap invis guesses and linken holders without direct targeting'], ['tip', 'canceling teleportation mid cast costs nothing, no cooldown and no mana, fake the rotation'], ['tip', 'wrath bounces a fixed count and each hit beyond the first adds damage, cast with vision across the map'], ['tip', 'the scepter wrath entangles every enemy it hits, a root and disarm bind scaling with the bounce'], ['counter', 'hold your disable for the end of the teleport animation, the cast is long and fully visible']] },
    { identity: 'sustain offlane core that outlasts burst and deletes tanky cores with reaper scythe', why: 'sustain core that outlasts burst from the offlane, reaper deletes tanky cores, favored into treant and tiny', how: 'pulse sustain through harass, farm to rad, scythe the tank in every fight', when: 'strong mid game once rad and shard land, dies to heal cut timings', build: 'rad, shard, consecrated wraps, lotus, bkb, heart, shiva', timings: [['rad', 16], ['shard', 20]], tech: ['bloodseeker and kotl are the vetoes, heal cut and mana drain kill the sustain plan', 'heartstopper wins long fights, never fight into AA'], mechanics: [['tip', 'sadist regen triggers on any unit dying, wards, buildings, denies, never illusions'], ['tip', 'death pulse lands on invis and fogged targets, no vision needed'], ['tip', 'ghost shroud blanks physical damage even from spells, omnislash and quill spray whiff'], ['counter', 'grave and false promise undo the scythe, sd and od banishes steal the window'], ['counter', 'he takes bonus magic damage inside ghost shroud, bait it before dumping nukes'], ['counter', 'vessel, skadi, and ice blast cut his healing, stack them before dueling him']] },
    { identity: 'reflect punish soft support, vendetta stalks picks from invis, impale lines the stun through their team, spiked carapace turns their nukes into self stuns', why: 'soft support stalker, favored into techies and shadow fiend lines, vetoed by luna and zeus long range spam, the carapace flips every spell trade', how: 'vendetta the pick from fog, impale the stacked lineup, carapace their retaliation, drain the caster with the strike, vanish off the map again', when: 'absent from lane once vendetta lands, mid game pick machine, late the invis sets up stuns instead of burst', build: 'essence distiller, blink, force, shard, aether lens, agh, dagon 5', timings: [['essence distiller', 16], ['blink', 26]], tech: ['luna, zeus, and invoker are the vetoes, long range spell spam outranges the stalk combo', 'techies, shadow fiend, and skywrath style lines are the free wins, paper backs fold to the stalk burst'], mechanics: [['tip', 'use vendetta invis for positioning, land the impale on their stack, the spikes stun the whole line'], ['tip', 'carapace negates and reflects one damage instance per source, stuns whoever hit you'], ['tip', 'carapace can be cast inside vendetta without dropping the invis, run into their spell spam for free stuns'], ['tip', 'late game vendetta\'s invis and speed are for impale positioning, the bonus damage matters less'], ['counter', 'do not retaliate after his combo, the carapace reflects and stuns whoever damages him, just walk away'], ['counter', 'carapace reflects once per source on a short buff, bait it out then commit your damage']] },
    { identity: 'orb burn mid, arcane orb turns the spare mana into pure damage, astral imprisonment banishes a body and drains its mana, essence flux feeds the pool off the casts, sanity\'s eclipse drops the whole clump on the mana gap', why: 'dedicated pos 2, the orb scales off the pool without items and the eclipse deletes the shallow mana pools, favored into the paper mana lines and the immobile mids, vetoed by the illusion flood and the mana burn crew', how: 'imprison the runner or the threatening core, orb the wave and the hero, hold the eclipse for the clumped shallow pools', when: 'lane dominance off the imprison and the orb poke, mid game astral picks and eclipse fights, late the orb burns everything on the map, starves when the mana burn and the floods stack', build: 'meteor hammer, midas, pike, bkb, sphere, sheepstick, devastator', timings: [['meteor hammer', 10], ['midas', 12]], tech: ['phantom lancer and nyx are the vetoes, the flood blanks the single target and the mana burn guts the pool', 'shadow fiend and timbersaw are the free wins, the eclipse pays the full drop on their shallow mana pools'], mechanics: [['tip', 'manually casting the orb onto heroes draws no creep aggro, the autocast orb does'], ['tip', 'the astral imprisonment jails roshan too'], ['tip', 'the astral steals the mana through spell immunity without the banish landing'], ['tip', 'astral the enemy before the eclipse, the mana gap widens and the drop pays more'], ['tip', 'the eclipse damages the banished bodies still inside the astral prison'], ['tip', 'the shard astral frees an ally to walk out of the chrono, the hole, the arena, and the kinetic field']] },
    { identity: 'swashbuckling roll mid, swashbuckle dashes and slashes through the wave, shield crash hops the clump and armors the engage, lucky shot procs the strip and the slow, rolling thunder bowls the whole fight out of position', why: 'dedicated pos 2, the innate halves the proc rolls held against him and the roll turns their formation inside out through the mid game, favored into proc reliant cores and clumped melee lines, vetoed by the rupture and soulbind pins and the root crew', how: 'swashbuckle the wave and the hero, crash the clump for the barrier, roll through their lines and bowl the cores out of position, shield crash the cliff mid roll and keep the ball moving', when: 'lane trades off the swashbuckle poke, mid game roll windows flip every standing fight, late the slashes and the proc luck snowball, dies when the lockdown stacks up', build: 'mage slayer, shard, shiva, octarine, disperser, abyssal blade, blessing', timings: [['mage slayer', 17], ['shard', 26]], tech: ['bloodseeker and grimstroke are the vetoes, the rupture bleeds the roll and the soulbind pins it in place', 'faceless void, troll warlord, and phantom assassin style proc carries are the free wins, the innate halves the proc odds they hold'], mechanics: [['tip', 'swashbuckle slashes carry true strike and land through disarms'], ['tip', 'swashbuckle and shield crash count as forced movement, climb the cliffs, pass through trees, and break the kinetic field walls'], ['tip', 'every item works mid roll, blink keeps the ball rolling and the cyclone self cast drops every bump on one body'], ['tip', 'the roll bounces off cogs, fissures, ice shards, and the map furniture, never off the towers or the ancient'], ['counter', 'the soulbind style leashes that pierce immunity spin the ball in place, the roll burns out mid lane'], ['counter', 'break kills the luck innate, silver edge and the break carriers turn every proc back on']] },
    { identity: 'crit carry, stifling dagger slows and chips the range, blink strike closes on the runner, blur fades her from the right clicks, coup de grace rolls the crits through the fight', why: 'dedicated pos 1, the blink strike converts every pick chance and the crits delete the paper cores, favored into the attack reliant lines without the true sight, vetoed by the aoe crew and the carapace turns', how: 'dagger the runner, blink strike the commit, blur through their focus and let the crits pick the kill order', when: 'dagger pickoffs from the early ranks, mid game blink windows open every rotation, late the crits two shot the supports, falls off when the evasion counters arrive', build: 'bfury, desolator, bkb, monkey king bar, satanic, nullifier, abyssal blade', timings: [['bfury', 15], ['desolator', 21]], tech: ['elder titan, brewmaster, and nyx are the vetoes, the natural order and the split blur the strike and the carapace turns the crit around', 'shadow fiend and huskar style paper farms are the free wins, the blur halves their swings and the crits cash them'], mechanics: [['tip', 'the dagger is an instant attack, it lands through disarms with true strike and rolls the modifiers when it hits'], ['tip', 'the blur active is no invisibility, the minimap icon goes and single target spells cannot find her, the cloaked model stays in sight'], ['tip', 'activating blur disjoints the incoming projectiles'], ['tip', 'the scepter fan of knives pierces the debuff immunity and the bkb'], ['tip', 'the scepter fan of knives shreds the illusion floods, the damage rolls off max health'], ['tip', 'the blade mail reflect stops at debuff immunity, the bkb body cashes the crits safe'], ['counter', 'the accuracy buys hit her through the evasion, mkb and bloodthorn pay the toll']] },
    { identity: 'illusion flood carry that overwhelms single target drafts', why: 'dedicated pos 1, illusion flood blanks single target drafts, favored into drow and SF style single target lines', how: 'lane with lance spam, farm to manta, fight with illusions tanking, split with doppel when they group', when: 'spikes once manta lands, scales into a late game monster with heart and stacked illusions', build: 'manta, skadi, shard, bloodthorn, heart, butterfly, blessing', timings: [['manta', 17], ['skadi', 31]], tech: ['sven is the loudest veto, leshrac and elder titan eat the flood with aoe', 'mars, SF, drow style single target drafts are the free wins, count their clear before locking'], mechanics: [['tip', 'the brighter doppel illusion takes full damage, group it and bait them onto the fake'], ['tip', 'doppel dispels everything manta would, roots and silences lock the cast entirely'], ['tip', 'doppel forces your landing spot, it outranks glimpse and x marks repositioning'], ['tip', 'juxtapose multiplies off wards not buildings, serpent wards and tombstone feed the flood'], ['counter', 'rupture, viper strike, maledict survive doppel and tag the real one'], ['counter', 'mjollnir static shield rolls on every illusion swing, the army chips itself']] },
    { identity: 'cog control hard support that hooks the pick, cages the fight and flares the map from anywhere', why: 'hard support pick holder, the hook starts every skirmish and the cogs close it, the flare hunts the whole map, favored into channel lines and immobile supports, vetoed by swarm bodies that eat the cogs', how: 'flare for vision and lane pressure, hook the isolated target, cage them with the battery running and hold the trap', when: 'spikes with the early hook tempo and first item timings, falls off when dispels and mass saves arrive late', build: 'essence distiller, vessel, blade mail, force, blink, glimmer, lotus', timings: [['essence distiller', 17], ['vessel', 21]], tech: ['phantom lancer and nature\'s prophet are the vetoes, swarms eat the cogs and block the hook', 'witch doctor and crystal maiden style channel lines are the free wins, the hook picks them every fight'], mechanics: [['tip', 'attacking your own cog punts it a full stretch ahead, shove the wall where you want it'], ['tip', 'each cog is a ward body with its own vision, punch one onto a cliff to scout or deward for free'], ['tip', 'the hook latches onto any unit it touches, allies, neutral creeps, even roshan, ride it out of a gank'], ['counter', 'the cog shocks hit the bodies outside the ring and drain their mana, hug the middle to stay safe'], ['counter', 'he flares globally to snipe regen from anywhere, keep salve and clarity use quiet against him'], ['counter', 'the flare aims at a point, stand still a beat after you break vision and he has to guess where you went']] },
    { identity: 'spell stealing soft support, telekinesis lifts and repositions any body, fade bolt strips the wave\'s damage, spell steal turns their fight plan against them', why: 'dedicated soft support, the lift answers every initiator and the steal vetoes one spell from every fight, favored into telegraphed ult lines, vetoed by the instant silence crew', how: 'lift the initiator before their spell, bolt the wave, wait out the big spell and steal it, re-aim the landing spot until the last tick', when: 'lane bolt poke from the first ranks, mid fights hinge on the steal timing, late the stolen ults decide the stand', build: 'essence distiller, blink, aether lens, glimmer, force, shard, aeon disk', timings: [['essence distiller', 15], ['blink', 23]], tech: ['silencer, skywrath, and drow are the vetoes, the instant silence cuts the lift and the steal', 'enigma, tidehunter, and sand king style ult lines are the free wins, one steal deletes their whole fight plan'], mechanics: [['tip', 'keep re-aiming the landing point until the drop, the body lands wherever the last click pointed'], ['tip', 'fade bolt never bounces to bodies you cannot see, fog and invis break the chain'], ['tip', 'every bounce shaves the bolt\'s damage, open on the ranged creep so the last hit lands near full power'], ['tip', 'stolen spells inherit his quick cast point, slow windups like split earth snap off at his tempo'], ['tip', 'stolen spell cooldowns persist, dumping a stolen ravage for fun costs the next fight you steal it for'], ['counter', 'he always steals the last spell cast, dump a cheap cover spell right after the big one']] },
    { identity: 'chain disable roaming soft support, hex blanks any hero, shackles lock the channel, serpent wards melt towers, fowl play cheats death', why: 'dedicated pos 4, hex first in the gank order holds any pick and the ward ring sieges every objective he roams to, favored into zeus and undying lines, vetoed by lancer swarms and lich poke', how: 'roam with the hex, hex the pick first, shackle holds it, shock the runner and the wave, ward the mid game objectives, deny the spent wards', when: 'lane kill threat once hex lands, roams set picks across the map, mid ward sieges take every objective, late hex chains anchor the fights', build: 'blink, aether lens, glimmer, force, shard, cyclone, refresher', timings: [['blink', 20], ['aether lens', 25]], tech: ['phantom lancer, bounty hunter, and lich are the vetoes, illusions and spam swarm past the single target locks', 'zeus, undying, and skywrath style lines are the free wins, paper bodies die inside the hex shackle chain'], mechanics: [['tip', 'ether shock reaches far past its cast range through the cone, cast it on the ranged creep to clip the runner'], ['tip', 'hex is instant cast, kills illusions on touch, and is a silence mute disarm break in one'], ['tip', 'hex has no cast point and out-ranges shackles, hex first in the gank order'], ['tip', 'drop the ward ring straight onto a hero, the circle blocks pathing and traps them inside'], ['counter', 'serpent ward attacks are not affected by damage block, block items do not mitigate them'], ['counter', 'shackles is channeled, keep a stun or silence ready to break the link off your ally']] },
    { identity: 'sprint offlane hunter that crushes the fight open, bashes the runner and hazes the target for the whole team to run down', why: 'offlane tempo core, the sprint hunts every rotation and the haze strips armor and true sights the runner, favored into invis and mobile carry lines, vetoed by the kite crew and haze dispels', how: 'sprint the rotation, crush the clump, bash the locked body, haze the runner and collapse the team onto it', when: 'sprint ganks from the first ranks, spikes with the early tempo buys mid game, hunts the roshan windows, falls off when the kite and saves arrive', build: 'midas, shard, bkb, harpoon, lotus, assault, nullifier', timings: [['midas', 15], ['shard', 21]], tech: ['razor, viper, and drow are the vetoes, static link and the range war strip the melee plan', 'riki, clinkz, and tinker style fades are the free wins, the haze lights up and runs down every slipping body'], mechanics: [['tip', 'cast the sprint mid teleport channel, the channel holds and he lands already moving'], ['tip', 'the crush puddle and the haze trail both count as river, the sprint river bonuses pay inside them'], ['tip', 'the bash counter builds on creeps and never expires, buildings and wards never count or eat the proc'], ['tip', 'skull basher and abyssal blade bashes are dead on him, the game allows only the deep bash'], ['counter', 'the sprint buff wipes off with any basic dispel, purge him mid dash to cut the chase'], ['counter', 'the haze wipes off with any basic dispel, lotus, greaves, and manta strip it unless the undispellable talent is in']] },
    { identity: 'melee carry stealing stats with essence shift, dark pact self-dispel, shadow dance invis roaming and escape', why: 'dedicated pos 2, essence shift snowballs every fight, favored into treant and soft support lines', how: 'dark pact the dust and track, pounce the leash, shadow dance resets the map', when: 'spikes once mage slayer lands, monster late with disperser and skadi off stolen stats', build: 'mage slayer, blink, shard, bkb, silver edge, disperser, skadi', timings: [['mage slayer', 19], ['blink', 23]], tech: ['grimstroke and kunkka veto, visage familiars reveal the dance', 'dark pact dispels track and dust but never silences, steal stats off the tank then leave'], mechanics: [['tip', 'every dark pact tick is a strong dispel, it rips stuns off you'], ['tip', 'pounce leash cancels tps and most mobility, it functions like a root'], ['tip', 'dance regen drops when enemy vision touches you, use it to sweep their wards'], ['counter', 'never stun into dark pact, the ticks purge it, wait the spell out then disable'], ['counter', 'break kills essence shift and dance regen, silver edge break never dispels'], ['counter', 'bloodseeker owns him, no pact off rupture, thirst true sights the dance']] },
    { identity: 'global haunt scaler that punishes squishy backlines', why: 'dedicated scaling pos 1, free win into sniper and drow style ranged carries that haunt deletes', how: 'farm to rad, farm both jungles, haunt fights that already started, never initiate', when: 'weak till rad, strong through the mid game, scales into a late game monster', build: 'rad, manta, skadi, bloodthorn, butterfly, abyssal blade, nullifier', timings: [['rad', 18], ['manta', 25]], tech: ['undying, necro, and invoker visible means no spectre, the tank plan dies first', 'haunt executes the backline, dispersion punishes physical burst'], mechanics: [['tip', 'dagger grants shared vision of everyone it hits, pings invis spots without true sight'], ['tip', 'the trail\'s free pathing lingers 1 second off the edge, cliff out behind you'], ['tip', 'dispersion reflects before reductions, armor and barriers never soften it'], ['counter', 'hug creeps when she shadow steps, the illusion damage is desolate only early']] },
    { identity: 'roaming zip mid, static remnant clones zone the lane, electric vortex drags the pick, overload charges every cast, ball lightning rips across the map and out again', why: 'dedicated pos 2, the zip hunts the whole map and the overload tempo snowballs every cast into a pick, favored into sniper and drow style immobile backlines, vetoed by silence chains and mana burn', how: 'remnant the lane, vortex the pick out of the wave, overload every cast, ball onto the backline, chain the zips home before their answers land', when: 'lane poke off remnant zones, kill windows once the zip unlocks, mid game hunt tempo off every rotation and rune, dies when the silence and mana burn answers stack up', build: 'kaya and sange, bkb, sphere, devastator, bloodthorn, shard, sheepstick', timings: [['kaya and sange', 25], ['bkb', 28]], tech: ['anti mage, nyx, and silencer are the vetoes, mana break and the silence chains starve the zip economy', 'sniper, drow, and crystal maiden style paper lines are the free wins, the zip reaches every backline that cannot answer'], mechanics: [['tip', 'overload can load an attack already in the air, toss the long right click then cast and the hit lands charged'], ['tip', 'ball lightning disjoints projectiles the moment it is cast, zip as the stun flies to waste it'], ['tip', 'he counts as invulnerable for the whole flight, dot ticks, delayed stuns, and rupture damage all dodge mid zip'], ['tip', 'spells keep casting mid flight, remnant and vortex never wait for the landing'], ['counter', 'most of his damage is magic but it rides the right clicks, no landed hit means no overload payout'], ['counter', 'the zip drinks mana with every stretch, mana burn and drain starve him, anti mage feasts']] },
    { identity: 'melee strength carry with a cleave steroid and a single-target storm hammer stun, god strength ult turns teamfights', why: 'dedicated pos 1, cleave plus god strength ends teamfights, favored into SF and muerta', how: 'farm with cleave, hammer their carry, god strength behind warcry armor', when: 'online once mask of madness lands, ult windows decide fights, strongest through the mid and late game', build: 'mask of madness, bkb, daedalus, harpoon, monkey king bar, swift blink, satanic', timings: [['mask of madness', 10], ['bkb', 24]], tech: ['lycan, troll, ww are the vetoes', 'cleave eats illusion drafts, ghost scepter blanks the hammer dive, never ult into ghost timings'], mechanics: [['tip', 'god\'s strength multiplies strength damage only, raw green damage items do not get scaled'], ['tip', 'agh\'s storm hammer dispels ghost scepter and windrun in its aoe'], ['tip', 'agh\'s hammer ignores roots and leashes, the invulnerability walks him out of mars arena'], ['counter', 'the hammer is a disjointable projectile, any disjoint wastes the stun'], ['counter', 'basic dispels strip warcry off him and his team, only the shard version is protected'], ['counter', 'break shuts off great cleave, god\'s strength is an active buff break never touches']] },
    { identity: 'trap line soft support, proximity mines carpet the approaches, sticky bomb tags and slows the runner, blast off leaps the clump for the silence and the deny, remote mines turn the objective into a no go zone', why: 'dedicated pos 5, the carpet taxes every rotation and the blast off trades any gank into even ground, favored into the farm races that walk the mine tax, vetoed by the wave clear crew and the dive hunters', how: 'carpet the chokes and the jungle approaches, sticky the engaged body, blast off the clump for the silence, park the remotes on roshan and the push paths', when: 'mines own the early rotations, mid game the blast off silence feeds every follow up, late the remote carpets delete the push, falls behind when the true sight arrives and the waves clear the field', build: 'aether lens, glimmer, force, blink, yasha and kaya, sheepstick, octarine', timings: [['aether lens', 18], ['glimmer', 26]], tech: ['bounty hunter and nyx assassin are the vetoes, the track economy hunts the roam and the vendetta dive runs the paper frame down', 'shadow fiend, slark, and drow style farm races are the free wins, every approach and every retreat runs the mine tax'], mechanics: [['tip', 'blast off respects the height map, a jump over a cliff edge can land on the ledge instead of the marked circle'], ['tip', 'spells keep casting mid blast off flight, the sticky and the mine plant never wait for the landing'], ['tip', 'proximity mines hit buildings with distance falloff, plant them flush against the tower for the full damage'], ['counter', 'the armed proximity mines sit invisible until you cross the trigger ring'], ['counter', 'one right click kills an armed mine, the fast attacking carries clear them before they arm'], ['counter', 'cheap summons and illusions trip the carpets, feed the treants and spiderlings through the minefield first']] },
    { identity: 'refraction carry, the charge shell blanks the instance damage, meld vanishes into the armor reduction burst, psi blades spill the wave down the line, psionic traps watch every path and slow the runner', why: 'dedicated pos 1, refraction wins the lane trades and the meld turns every fog bank into a kill setup, favored into the paper lanes, vetoed by the summon floods and the wolf runs that outlast the shell', how: 'refraction the trade, meld the fog bank and the tower line, spill the wave through the front bodies, trap the approaches before the fight breaks', when: 'refraction owns the early trades, mid game the meld picks and the trap vision control the map, late the spill carries the fights, falls behind when the instance floods strip the shell', build: 'falcon blade, desolator, pike, daedalus, bkb, monkey king bar, swift blink', timings: [['falcon blade', 7], ['desolator', 15]], tech: ['phoenix, leshrac, and phantom lancer are the vetoes, the fire spirits strip the shell and the image floods run the paper frame down', 'natures prophet and shadow fiend lines are the free wins, the paper frames melt to the meld strikes'], mechanics: [['tip', 'refraction blocks the whole instance, the blink dagger and the regen items never break through the shell'], ['tip', 'meld has no cast or fade time, it disjoints the shots mid chase and the juke in fog leaves them chasing ghosts'], ['tip', 'the meld strike rides the psi blade spill, the armor reduction lands on every body the attack spills onto'], ['counter', 'overkill on one refraction layer never bleeds into the next, one big nuke peels exactly one charge'], ['counter', 'meld never breaks to stuns or silences, the knockback spells break it and the dust and sentries reveal it'], ['counter', 'the early sentries on the hill finish the meld ganks and clear her traps on your side']] },
    { identity: 'metamorphosis illusion carry, reflection turns every enemy into their own attacker, conjure image floods the map with bodies, metamorphosis turns the whole pack ranged, sunder flips the health scales at the brink', why: 'dedicated pos 1, the ranged illusion pack sieges towers faster than any carry defends, favored into melee and single target lines, vetoed by the area clear and magic burst crew', how: 'farm images on both sides of the map, meta the pack behind your team, reflection the clumped engage, sunder the diver at the brink', when: 'fragile lane that hides behind images, spikes hard once the image count stacks up, monster siege through the mid game, dies to the coordinated burst', build: 'falcon blade, manta, skadi, pike, butterfly, bkb, daedalus', timings: [['falcon blade', 7], ['manta', 18]], tech: ['leshrac, earthshaker, and sand king are the vetoes, the area clear wipes the image pack before the siege pays', 'sniper, drow ranger, and medusa style passive lines are the free wins, the ranged pack outpushes and outranges everything slow'], mechanics: [['tip', 'his own illusions only hold metamorphosis inside the transform aura, walk the real hero with the siege'], ['tip', 'sunder never touches debuff immune targets, a bkb on the low hero blanks the swap'], ['tip', 'sunder floors both bodies at a minimum share of max health, two low targets both rise to the floor'], ['tip', 'sunder sets health instead of dealing damage or healing, the swap still lands through heal cuts like ice blast'], ['counter', 'reflection copies item auras onto its illusions, your radiance and cuirass auras end up working for him'], ['counter', 'huge armor on a paper thin health pool, magic damage shreds him and every illusion he owns']] },
    { identity: 'chainsaw brawl offlaner, timber chain whips him between the trees, whirling death pure nukes the clump and strips the primary attribute, reactive armor stacks the regen front, chakram saws the fight open and grinds the wounded', why: 'dedicated pos 3, the chain crosses terrain on tree money and the armor front outlasts every right click line, favored into strength cores and tree heavy ground, vetoed by the mana drain and break crew', how: 'chain the tree through the fight, whirl the clump and strip the attribute, armor up under the focus, saw the runner and hold the blade on the retreat line', when: 'lane bully off the chain poke, mid game dives live forever behind the armor, late falls off as the raw damage outscales the stack, starves when the drain lands', build: 'kaya and sange, lotus, bkb, shiva, heart, shard, sheepstick', timings: [['kaya and sange', 20], ['lotus', 27]], tech: ['silencer is the veto, the instant silence strands the saw mid flight, ancient apparition only pinches, the ice blast trims the armor regen while the crawl keeps the saw ahead', 'strength and universal cores are the free wins, the whirl strips the primary attribute every single fight'], mechanics: [['counter', 'strength cores eat the whirl attribute strip all lane, the primary drain leaves them swinging softer'], ['tip', 'tank a neutral camp before the dive to preload the reactive armor stacks, the regen front walks in built'], ['tip', 'the innate pays mana back for every tree destroyed, the saws and the whirl refund the chain economy'], ['tip', 'the saw taxes both directions, return the chakram while the runner sits in it for the second pass'], ['counter', 'the silence locks him dead with the saw out, disarmed by the chakram and unable to return it'], ['counter', 'stun him after the chain comes out and he stops mid flight, the cast burns anyway']] },
    { identity: 'avalanche toss combo carry, rocks pulse stun in an area, toss grabs and hurls any unit, tree grab swings splash, grow inflates the stats', why: 'dedicated carry, favored into spirit breaker and ember spirit lines, vetoed by phantom lancer and luna', how: 'lead the avalanche, toss the nearest body through it, grab a tree for the splash, grow into the siege', when: 'lane kill threat once the combo lands, mid game burst pickoffs, late game building crusher', build: 'silver edge, harpoon, bkb, daedalus, assault, monkey king bar, swift blink', timings: [['silver edge', 25], ['harpoon', 29]], tech: ['phantom lancer, luna, and windranger are the vetoes, illusions and split pressure outpace the combo tempo', 'spirit breaker, lion, and ember spirit style lines are the free wins, single bodies eat the full combo'], mechanics: [['tip', 'avalanche pulses damage and stun in intervals, lead the target and the rocks catch walkers'], ['tip', 'toss disables whoever is thrown, and avalanche deals double damage to the tossed unit'], ['tip', 'debuff immune enemies can never be thrown, but you can still toss something at them'], ['tip', 'toss always grabs the nearest unit around tiny, allies included, mash it in a crowd'], ['tip', 'toss grabs units inside the grab radius even from fog, invisible units are the exception'], ['counter', 'the avalanche area keeps stunning, walking in late still eats the rocks']] },
    { identity: 'brawl roam soft support, ice shards walls the choke and scouts the fog, snowball wraps the team into an invulnerable roll, tag team feeds every allied swing, walrus punch launches the crit that breaks the channel', why: 'dedicated pos 4, the snowball commits any ally through the burst and the punch deletes the paper core, favored into the immobile farm races, vetoed by the tanky fronts that shrug the roll', how: 'shard the choke before the fight, roll the team onto the target, tag team the commit, punch the channeler or the runner, shard the retreat line on the way out', when: 'roam tempo from the opening ranks, snowball picks through the mid game, late the punch and the tag team swings carry the brawl, falls behind when the fronts out-tank the commit', build: 'blink, vessel, glimmer, force, agh, lotus, bkb', timings: [['blink', 19], ['vessel', 21]], tech: ['bounty hunter, dragon knight, dark seer, and sven are the vetoes, the track hunts the melee roam and the tanky fronts shrug the snowball', 'shadow fiend, huskar, and nature\'s prophet style paper farms are the free wins, the snowball reaches every immobile frame and the punch launches it'], mechanics: [['tip', 'everyone wrapped in the snowball is invulnerable and hidden, the ball rides out the burst mid roll'], ['tip', 'target neutrals or lane creeps with the snowball when escaping, the ball drops you at a predictable safe spot'], ['tip', 'spells keep casting mid snowball, prime the shards and the tag team before the ball breaks'], ['tip', 'tag team\'s bonus damage is green damage, cleave, lifesteal, and crit all pay off it, always enable it before the punch'], ['tip', 'walrus punch breaks channels through debuff immunity and ignores spell block, hold it for the teleport out'], ['counter', 'tusk cannot cast snowball while rooted or leashed, hold the root for his commit']] },
    { identity: 'swipe stack brawl carry, earthshock stomps the clump and slows it, overpower bursts the swings at max speed, fury swipes deepen with every hit on the same body, enrage shakes the debuffs off and shrugs the damage through the commit', why: 'dedicated pos 1, the swipes scale off swings and the pit opens on demand, favored into the paper cores and the immobile front lines, vetoed by the clone flood and the kite crew, no chase without the blink', how: 'stomp the clump, blink onto the runner, hold the swipes on one body, pop the enrage under the focus and take the objective with the stack alive', when: 'pit windows from the early timings, mid game objectives and siege spikes behind the stack, late falls off when the kites, saves, and disarms arrive', build: 'bfury, bkb, monkey king bar, abyssal blade, satanic, swift blink, blessing', timings: [['bfury', 14], ['bkb', 28]], tech: ['meepo is the veto, the clone flood blanks the swipes and the poof burst deletes the grounded ball', 'shadow fiend and monkey king are the free wins, the paper cores stand still for the swipe stack'], mechanics: [['tip', 'the earthshock leap hops cliffs both ways and jumps clear of the kinetic field'], ['tip', 'the overpower buff outlasts its cooldown, cast it early before the gank or the pit so the second cast waits in the chamber'], ['tip', 'casting enrage carries a basic dispel that wipes dots, slows, blinds, and roots, the scepter upgrade walks out of the stuns'], ['tip', 'the swipes work on roshan, the pit solo opens on demand'], ['counter', 'break only stops the new swipe stacks, the standing stack keeps paying its bonus'], ['counter', 'the overpower burst wipes off with any basic purge, the shadow demon purge bites through the enrage plan']] },
    { identity: 'poison zone hard support, venomous gale slows the lane from range, poison sting stacks the chase tax, plague wards flood the fights and the towers, poison nova tags every body near him', why: 'dedicated pos 5, the ward flood zones every objective and the gale owns the chase lanes, favored into the paper frames that stand in the poison, vetoed by the image floods and the spread drafts that run past the wards', how: 'gale the runner from the fog, ward the choke and the pit before the fight, sting the body the carries chase, nova the clump as it commits', when: 'gale picks land roams through the early game, mid game the ward carpets tax every objective, late the nova chips the whole team, falls behind when the clears and the heals answer', build: 'vessel, mekansm, glimmer, force, cyclone, shard, agh', timings: [['vessel', 18], ['mekansm', 25]], tech: ['phantom lancer, juggernaut, and outworld destroyer are the vetoes, the image floods and the astral banks run past the ward zones', 'shadow fiend, monkey king, and kez lines are the free wins, the paper frames stand in the poison'], mechanics: [['tip', 'no hero forces the wards to swing, stop them empty handed and park the spares on the cliffs out of sight'], ['tip', 'the ward attacks carry half damage poison sting with the full slow, every body the ward touches pays the chase tax'], ['tip', 'the wards see 800 both day and night, spam them for vision across every approach'], ['tip', 'the spread projectiles carry every debuff venomancer applied on the target and duplicate them on the secondary bodies'], ['counter', 'the venom debuffs peel to a basic dispel, manta and lotus wipe the whole kit until the snakebite talent'], ['counter', 'the sting dot is hp removal, it never cancels the blink daggers or the regen items']] },
    { identity: 'poison kite offlaner, poison attack arrows layer the slow and the burn on every body, nethertoxin pools the ground and grinds the clump inside it, corrosive skin returns the damage and shrugs the magic, viper strike glues the runner and switches its passives off, nosedive dives the fight from the sky', why: 'dedicated pos 3, the lane poison starves every melee core and the skin flips the spell lanes around, favored into passive front heroes and the right click grinders, vetoed by the illusion flood crew and the unslowable runs', how: 'layer the arrows on the lane body, drop the toxin pool over the clump and the objective, hold the strike for the runner, dive the committed fight with the nosedive and stand the ground the skin wins', when: 'lane poison from the opening minutes, toxin zones hold every objective through the mid game, the nosedive and the strike pick the late fights, falls off when the burst and the saves outscale the grind', build: 'mage slayer, pike, blink, manta, bkb, shiva, shard', timings: [['mage slayer', 16], ['pike', 24]], tech: ['meepo and lycan are the vetoes, the clone flood and the unslowable pack blank the poison kite', 'bristleback and huskar are the free wins, the strike break switches the passives off and the poison grind runs them down'], mechanics: [['tip', 'manually casting the poison arrow onto heroes draws no creep aggro, the autocast arrow does'], ['tip', 'viper strike lands whole through spell immunity, the slow and the break both hold on the bkb body'], ['tip', 'the shard poison arrows strip building armor, the debuff rides the towers'], ['tip', 'the nosedive crosses cliffs both ways and the flight stretches with the distance'], ['counter', 'every damage tick he takes poisons the attacker back and he carries the magic resist, the dot wars and radiance style burns feed him'], ['counter', 'the viper strike missile disjoints, and roots and leashes lock the nosedive entirely']] },
    { identity: 'ranged latch carry, shackleshot pins a body to whatever stands behind it, powershot arrows the wave, windrun dodges the dive, focus fire shreds the locked target', why: 'dedicated pos 1, the latch sets every kill and focus fire deletes the pinned body, favored into lifestealer and ursa style commit melee, vetoed by lancer floods and the blink hex crew', how: 'shackle the runner to a creep or tree, powershot the wave and the fog lines, windrun their dive, focus fire the pinned body', when: 'lane harass off the arrow and shackle threat, mid game pick machine off the latch, focus fire cracks towers and rosh, dies the moment the chain lock lands', build: 'mjollnir, bkb, pike, hydras breath, sphere, daedalus, satanic', timings: [['mjollnir', 20], ['bkb', 27]], tech: ['phantom lancer, naga siren, and lion are the vetoes, floods outbody the fire and the instant hex locks the windrun', 'lifestealer, ursa, and huskar style lines are the free wins, committed melee eats the latch and the fire'], mechanics: [['tip', 'the shackle latch angle is computed from where the shot was cast, not where windranger stands when it lands'], ['tip', 'shackleshot latches fogged and invisible units, park a creep to pin the melded templar assassin as the second body'], ['tip', 'windrun dodges every incoming attack, towers included, even a projectile already in flight rolls the dodge on impact'], ['tip', 'focus fire grants no vision on the target, drop a quick powershot to hold the fogged runner in sight'], ['counter', 'focus fire strings many small hits together, damage block like vanguard or crimson guard eats the window'], ['counter', 'venomancer snakebite bursts on every attack she lands, it wrecks a focus fire commitment']] },
    { identity: 'curse setup hard support, arctic burn flies over vision lines, splinter blast chases through fog, cold embrace blanks physical focus, winter\'s curse turns their carry on the team', why: 'hard support playmaker, favored into shadow fiend and tiny lines, vetoed by arc warden clones and lancer swarms, the curse flips every crowd control war', how: 'burn fat hp from arctic flight, splinter out of fog, embrace the focused core, curse the clumped engage, let their carry do the killing', when: 'lane bully with burn harass, mid curse setups decide fights, late embrace keeps the core alive through physical burst', build: 'blink, glimmer, holy locket, aether lens, shard, lotus, aeon disk', timings: [['blink', 22], ['glimmer', 27]], tech: ['arc warden, phantom lancer, and necrophos are the vetoes, clones and sustained heals blunt the curse', 'shadow fiend, tiny, and kez style lines are the free wins, clumped squishy folds to curse plus splinter'], mechanics: [['tip', 'arctic burn attacks burn a share of the target\'s current hp per second and slow it, hunt the fattest bodies'], ['tip', 'splinter blast leaves the primary target completely unaffected, only the flying splinters damage and slow'], ['tip', 'cold embrace cocoons an ally, healing it while blocking every physical damage instance'], ['tip', 'winters curse grows longer per enemy caught, taunted creeps add duration too, aim for the clumped wave'], ['tip', 'the frozen target and its taunted attackers are immune to enemy damage, only auroth and her units can hurt them'], ['counter', 'never stand near a cursed ally, the curse forces everyone in the radius to attack the frozen teammate']] },
    { identity: 'voodoo curse hard support, paralyzing cask pinballs the stun through the wave, voodoo restoration aura heals the push, maledict dooms the wounded, death ward shreds the clump', why: 'hard support lane anchor, cask harass and the heal aura win the sustain war, maledict turns every trade into a kill threat, death ward melts the clumped fights, favored into committed melee lines, vetoed by long range poke and free sustain', how: 'cask the wave after the melee creeps fall, heal the lane with the aura, maledict the traded target, ward the clump from max range behind fog', when: 'lane cask threat from the first ranks, maledict kills after every trade, mid death wards decide the roshan fights, late the aura holds the siege', build: 'vessel, glimmer, blink, shard, force, aether lens, aeon disk', timings: [['vessel', 20], ['glimmer', 24]], tech: ['zeus, necrophos, and silencer are the vetoes, long range poke and free sustain blunt the cask and the curse', 'ursa, sven, and troll warlord style melee lines are the free wins, committed bodies eat the pinball and the maledict ticks'], mechanics: [['tip', 'paralyzing cask bounces to units hidden in fog, the pinball keeps hunting unseen bodies'], ['tip', 'cask stuns hardest when the wave thins, pop the enemy once the lone ranged creep is the only bounce anchor'], ['tip', 'death ward can attack creep-hero bodies like brewlings, familiars, and the golem'], ['tip', 'toggling voodoo restoration never breaks the death ward channel, keep the heal running through the ult'], ['counter', 'maledict punishes health lost since it landed, healing yourself softens every later tick'], ['counter', 'one stun, silence, or banish ends the death ward channel, dedicate someone to the cancel']] },
  ],
